  "ranking_policy": "Trades are ordered by verdict (sensible, sensible with concerns, unlikely to be mutually attractive, asset-fair without a lineup gain, one-sided, incomplete), then by Pareto front over three separately measured axes: the smaller side's projected starting-lineup gain (points), the asset-package ratio (smaller package as a share of the larger, points above replacement) and certainty (fewer injury and missing-data flags). Within a verdict a trade is in a later front only when another trade is at least as good on all three and better on one. Within a front the view's own measure decides (e.g. the smaller side's gain), then the exact search order. No axis is converted into another and nothing estimates whether a manager would accept.",
